# Taurean Mauler's ability resolves even if the spell that caused it is countered (the ruling; CR 603.2, 113.7a): Bot2 casts a
# Mox Sapphire and the Mauler's trigger goes on the stack above it. In response Bot1 counters the Mox with Counterspell, which
# resolves first; the trigger then still resolves, Bot1 accepts, and the Mauler gets its +1/+1 counter (3/3). Bot1's own
# Counterspell triggers nothing.

[Bot1 Deck]
Taurean Mauler
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Counterspell
Mountain
Mountain x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Island x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Taurean Mauler.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Taurean Mauler.Power = 2
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
? Stack.Count = 2
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Counterspell.Cast(Stack.Mox Sapphire)
? Stack.Count = 3
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Graveyard = Mox Sapphire
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Accept

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Taurean Mauler.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Taurean Mauler.Power = 3
Bot2.Battlefield =
Bot1.Graveyard = Counterspell; Black Lotus
